  "limitation_statement_draft": "Clinical-only baseline limitation (P0-4 audit, computed not assumed): the patient-level covariates deposited with the three efficacy cohorts are not mutually harmonizable. GSE165252 (PERFECT) deposits no patient-level covariate of any kind (only tissue, treatment arm and response), the IMvigor210 pData contains no patient age (its 'Sample.age' column is a sample-timing category), and the staging constructs differ (IMvigor210 TCGA stage group vs GSE78220 AJCC M category). The covariate set common to all three cohorts is therefore empty, and the maximal set harmonizable between the training cohort (IMvigor210) and any external cohort is {sex, a crude advanced/metastatic-stage binary}, transportable only to GSE78220. On GSE165252 every clinical-only model necessarily degenerates to a constant (covariate-marginal) prediction with AUC exactly 0.5, so for that cohort prevalence-only is the strongest clinical baseline the deposited data permit. These constraints are properties of the deposited data, not modelling choices; a richer clinical baseline would require patient-level covariate tables from the trial sponsors/publications that are not part of the GEO deposits."
}